<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Salvador Sánchez Cerén</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1944">1944</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a> Sánchez Cerén is a Salvadoran former schoolteacher and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> commander of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/farabundo-marti-national-liberation-front">FMLN</a> during the civil war, and a signatory of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chapultepec-peace-accords">Chapultepec Peace Accords</a> of 1992. He served as vice-president from 2009 and as president from 2014 to 2019, the first former guerrilla to hold the office. He later went to live in Nicaragua.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/salvador-sanchez-ceren.jpg" alt="Salvador Sánchez Cerén" width="320" height="490" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Presidencia El Salvador from San Salvador, El Salvador, América Central · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Informe_de_Primer_a%C3%B1o_de_Gobierno_(18346856652)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
